**Key constraint:** Cannot hire additional managers or meaningfully reduce span of control (at best shed 3-4 reports). Rebalancing within the current management role is not a viable option.

**Frozen CoS role:** There is a frozen Chief of Staff role in the org. The traditional CoS work (budgets, operational rhythm, being a voice of the VP) is easy for the user. The opportunity is to evolve that frozen role into something more strategic — connecting portfolio governance, technical strategy, AI transformation, innovation, and org effectiveness."}

Edit {"replace_all":false,"file_path":"D:\lgcareer\email.md","old_string":"I wanted to share some thinking ahead of our conversation. I committed to a six-month introspection point when I took this role, and I want to be direct about what I'm seeing. The diagram below summarises where I've landed.","new_string":"I wanted to share some thinking ahead of our conversation. I committed to a six-month introspection point when I took this role, and I want to be upfront about why.

I have been through burnout before. I know what the trajectory looks like, and I can feel it forming again — not because the work is hard, but because the work does not use what I do best, and the strategic work I do take on goes unrecognised. I am raising this now because I want to get ahead of it, not react to it. I want to be in a role I can sustain and enjoy, and where the organisation gets the full return on what I bring.

With that context, here is where I've landed. The diagram below summarises it."}

